From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:45:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: edp: Program the v8 PCS lane drive levels

The v8 PCS has per-lane-pair drive level registers, LN0_DRV_LVL and
LN1_DRV_LVL, next to the AUX-less timing registers. The v8 combo PHY
programs its equivalents for DisplayPort, but the eDP PHY sequence
leaves them at whatever value they held before, so their setting
depends on what ran earlier.

Program both to 0x12, the TX drive level the sequence sets before the
PLL starts. The sequence that drives the Surface Laptop 8 panel at
5.4 Gbps programs the same value. Link training adjusts the drive level
in the TX lanes only, as before.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
index c974a398ada..98625c28ecb 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-edp.c
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@
 #define DP_PHY_LFPS_CYC                         0x00d8
 #define DP_PHY_AUXLESS_SETUP_CYC                0x00dc
 #define DP_PHY_AUXLESS_SILENCE_CYC              0x00e0
+#define DP_PHY_LN0_DRV_LVL                      0x00e4
+#define DP_PHY_LN1_DRV_LVL                      0x00e8
 #define DP_PHY_LDO_CFG                          0x00f0
 
 #define DP_PHY_STATUS                           0x00e0
@@ -1472,6 +1474,8 @@ static int qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v8(const struct qcom_edp *edp)
 {
 	writel(0x05, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX0_TX1_LANE_CTL);
 	writel(0x05, edp->edp + DP_PHY_TX2_TX3_LANE_CTL_V8);
+	writel(0x12, edp->edp + DP_PHY_LN0_DRV_LVL);
+	writel(0x12, edp->edp + DP_PHY_LN1_DRV_LVL);
 
 	return qcom_edp_configure_tx_pre_pll_v8_lanes(edp);
 }
